# Attack: same as 03 but with explicit `&` borrow. Must be REJECTED — and
# since D10(a) (decisions.md, ratified 2026-07-06) it is, at PARSE time: the
# `int &borrowed = ...` decl-sigil form of a local `&`-bind is illegal (one
# exclusive writer per place). Pre-D10 the parser silently discarded the
# sigil, `borrowed` was a value copy, and this "attack" was misclassified
# safe (printed 10).

void main():
    Vector[int] v = [10, 20, 30, 40]
    int &borrowed = v.get(0).unwrap()
    v.push(50)  # unreachable: the decl above is rejected
    print(borrowed)
